# Components Module Rules

## Purpose
Reusable React components including Shadcn UI components, form components, landing page sections, and custom UI elements.

## Entry Points
- `src/components/ui/**` - Shadcn UI base components
- `src/components/form/**` - Form components
- `src/components/LandingPage/**` - Landing page sections
- `src/components/magicui/**` - Magic UI components
- `src/components/NavBar.tsx` - Navigation component
- `src/components/Profile.tsx` - Profile component

## Allowed Imports
- `@/lib/utils` - Utility functions (cn, etc.)
- `@/components/ui/*` - Other UI components
- React and React DOM
- Radix UI primitives
- Framer Motion for animations
- Lucide React, Tabler Icons, React Icons
- React Hook Form for form components
- Zod for validation schemas

## Forbidden Imports
- `@/lib/db` - No database access in components
- `@/app/**` - No importing from app routes
- `@/utils/db/**` - No direct database utilities
- Node.js built-ins

## Coding Conventions

### Component Structure
- Use functional components with TypeScript
- Add `"use client"` directive for client components
- Use named exports for components
- Define props interfaces above component

### Shadcn UI Components
- Located in `src/components/ui/`
- Follow Shadcn UI patterns and conventions
- Use `cn()` utility for className merging
- Support variant props using `class-variance-authority`

### Form Components
- Use React Hook Form for form state
- Use Zod for validation schemas
- Use `@hookform/resolvers/zod` for validation
- Follow form component patterns from `src/components/form/`

### Styling
- Use TailwindCSS utility classes
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes
- Follow responsive design patterns (mobile-first)
- Use Shadcn UI components when available

### Component Example
```typescript
"use client";

import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

interface MyComponentProps {
  className?: string;
  children: React.ReactNode;
}

export function MyComponent({ className, children }: MyComponentProps) {
  return (
    <div className={cn("base-styles", className)}>
      {children}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Icons
- Use Lucide React as primary icon library
- Use Tabler Icons for additional icons
- Use React Icons for specific icon sets
- Import icons from their respective packages

## AI Hints
- Keep components focused and single-purpose
- Prefer composition over complex prop drilling
- Use TypeScript interfaces for all props
- Follow Shadcn UI component patterns
- Use TailwindCSS for all styling
- Make components reusable and composable
- Add `"use client"` only when using hooks or browser APIs
